WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.967
"Carbadox, the Carcinogenic Drug
Fed to U.S. Pigs but Banned in Other Countries"

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:10.640
In the late 1960s, carbadox,
a new feed additive

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:12.320
which promoted growth in chicks

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:15.440
was also found
to promote growth in pigs.

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:18.320
It is now fed to more than
40 percent of young pigs

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:19.920
in the United States,

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:21.840
not only to increase
rate of growth

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:24.560
but to control
diarrheal disease, too.

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:26.800
However, carbadox
is also a genotoxic

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:29.200
and mutagenic carcinogen
in animals.

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:31.360
More than 25 years ago,

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:33.600
the European Commission
banned the use of carbadox

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:34.720
in meat production

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:36.320
due to its possible
adverse effects

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:37.920
on human health.

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:40.160
Stating "it is not possible
to set a threshold

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:42.880
for a genotoxic
(DNA-damaging) additive

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:45.680
below which" there is no risk
to the consumer,

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:47.280
since even a small quantity

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:50.240
could provoke
a tumor-inducing mutation.

00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:51.920
Other countries followed.

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:54.400
Canada halted its sale
more than 20 years ago,

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:56.400
and the Food
and Agriculture Organization

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:58.400
and World Health Organization
joint committee

00:00:58.400 --> 00:00:59.840
on food additives

00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:03.440
decided there is
no acceptable intake amount.

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:05.840
So, why is a drug
banned in many countries

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:08.640
still being fed to pigs
in the United States?

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:11.440
Well, one reason
is that the drug maker

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:12.800
has been defending carbadox,

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:15.120
sold under
the brand name Mecadox,

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:16.880
since the U.S.
Food and Drug Administration

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:18.880
first proposed
rescinding its use

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:20.560
based on concerns
about the persistence

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:23.760
of carcinogenic residues
in meat.

00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:25.840
And no surprise
the National Pork Producers

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:28.400
oppose the FDA's proposal
to ban it,

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:29.520
likely because,

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:32.560
just as the drug company's
marketing brochure says:

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:36.640
"Bottom line, Mecadox can
help you market more pork"

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:38.480
and make them more money.

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:41.040
We're talking about more than
$20 million a year

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:43.680
with sales
continuing to increase.

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:46.160
The pork industry claims
that removing carbadox

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:49.120
would inevitably increase
use of other antibiotics

00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:52.480
and the likelihood
of antimicrobial resistance.

00:01:52.480 --> 00:01:55.280
If it really cared
about antibiotic resistance,

00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:58.320
maybe pork producers would
stop feeding millions of pounds

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:00.720
of medically important
antibiotics to pigs

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:03.200
every year
in the United States.

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:06.160
And carbadox can actually
activate dormant viruses

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:08.560
that can transfer
antibiotic-resistant genes

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:10.800
among bacteria.

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:12.720
This can lead
to bacterial whack-a-mole,

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:14.480
where using carbadox
in pig production

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:17.200
may help prevent
some bacterial infections

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:19.360
but can also lead
to the emergence of bacteria

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:21.200
that are resistant
to antibiotics

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:24.080
used in human medicine.

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:25.920
There's a stalemate at the FDA

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:27.680
as the drug maker
keeps battling

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:29.520
to continue selling carbadox,

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:32.240
and the FDA keeps conceding
to its demands.

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:35.840
As of November 2023,
there seemed to be some hope

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:38.720
of the FDA withdrawing carbadox
from the market,

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:41.440
but we are still waiting
on final word.

00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:43.200
In the meantime, carbadox,

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:45.600
with its 97.9 percent
likelihood

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:47.600
of causing cancer in humans,

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:49.040
is still banned
in many countries

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:50.320
around the world,

00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:52.400
and it's still
being fed to pigs

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:56.159
bound for the supermarket
in the United States.

